  "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate, we flip the sign of the imaginary part.\n\nIn the given number $z=7-9\\text{i},$ the imaginary part is $-9\\text{i}.$ Flipping the sign, we get $9\\text{i}.$\n\nTherefore, the complex conjugate is given by $\\overset{\u2015}{z}=7+9\\text{i}.$",
